values ('phys2-pv-special-processes', 'ap_physics_2', 'xy_series', 'PV diagram: the four special processes', 'PV: special processes', 'Isovolumetric, isobaric, isothermal and adiabatic from one starting state (figure 2 of 2)', 'Four named processes from the same starting state: vertical, horizontal, along the isotherm, and steeper than it.', 'A pressure-versus-volume diagram showing four processes leaving the same starting state. The isovolumetric process is a vertical line, because the volume does not change. The isobaric process is a horizontal line, because the pressure does not change. The isothermal process follows the isotherm, on which pressure times volume is constant. The adiabatic process starts at the same point but falls more steeply than the isotherm, because no energy is transferred thermally. Illustrative data.', 'volume V', 'pressure P', 'The adiabat is steeper than the isotherm through the same point: that is how the two are told apart.', true, null, '["Isovolumetric process", "Isobaric process", "Isothermal process", "Adiabatic process"]'::jsonb, '{"hide_axis_numbers": true, "x_range": [1.2, 4.6], "y_range": [0.0, 5.2], "series": [{"kind": "line", "style": "solid", "label": "isothermal", "points": [[2.0, 3.0], [2.01375, 2.97951582867784], [2.0275, 2.9593094944512948], [2.04125, 2.93937538273117], [2.055, 2.9197080291970803], [2.06875, 2.900302114803625], [2.0825, 2.881152460984394], [2.09625, 2.862254025044723], [2.11, 2.843601895734597], [2.12375, 2.825191288993526], [2.1375, 2.807017543859649], [2.15125, 2.789076118535735], [2.165, 2.771362586605081], [2.17875, 2.7538726333907055], [2.1925, 2.7366020524515395], [2.20625, 2.7195467422096318], [2.22, 2.7027027027027026], [2.23375, 2.686066032456631], [2.2475, 2.6696329254727473], [2.26125, 2.6533996683250414], [2.275, 2.6373626373626373], [2.28875, 2.621518296013108], [2.3025, 2.6058631921824102], [2.31625, 2.5903939557474365], [2.33, 2.575107296137339], [2.34375, 2.56], [2.3575, 2.545068928950159]